profile: minimodel.totem.v3
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
site: MiniModel.org
role: positive_anchor
mission: Build a Rust-first peer-to-peer tiny model package catalog and exchange where users verify and run model packages locally.
anchors:
  - Peer-to-peer or source-routed transfer, not hosted model-weight service.
  - Signed or checksum-bound model manifests.
  - Local Rust verification before TinyRustLM companion import.
  - Clear separation between catalog metadata, peer transfer, and local execution.
talisman_source: MiRust.com
agent_mutability: read_only_without_exact_human_artifact_and_operation_authorization

pre_publication_clean_slate_policy_id: pre-publication-clean-slate-v1
pre_publication_clean_slate_authority: "Treat this site and every consuming system as pre-publication dogfood, even when a development URL is publicly reachable. Until the human explicitly removes this authority, choose the best current architecture; full rewrites and clean contract replacements are authorized when they improve correctness, security, maintainability, performance, accessibility, or product quality."
pre_publication_replacement_completion_authority: "Verify replacements end to end, migrate every dogfood caller to one current contract, remove superseded implementation in the same completed change, and finish tests, documentation, security review, and cleanup before deployment. Preserve immutable receipts and historical failure evidence as audit truth, never as a promise to support obsolete product behavior."
documentation_integrity_policy_id: site-family-documentation-integrity-v1
documentation_site_role: catalog-discovery-product-with-user-developer-and-operator-documentation
documentation_integrity_authority: "Documentation is a first-class production surface. Keep catalog semantics, direct-P2P boundaries, identity and proof requirements, consent, privacy, security, failure states, operator procedures, integration contracts, limitations, and release material complete, technically rigorous, navigable, and current."
documentation_same_change_rule: "Update affected documentation, examples, schemas, diagrams, error behavior, cross-site links, version metadata, update history, and machine-readable release records in the same completed change as catalog or protocol behavior."
documentation_verification_rule: "Before publication, verify examples, links, navigation, accessibility, responsive rendering, contract references, public HTTPS readback, and agreement with MiniModel.MiRust.com and TinyRustLM surfaces."
documentation_truth_rule: "Distinguish proposed, implemented, locally tested, externally proven, deployed, degraded, stale, revoked, and unavailable behavior. Never promote P2P reachability, model quality, catalog activity, or publication from source, fixtures, local probes, packages, or reachable pages alone."
documentation_release_gate: "Do not publish an affected site when documentation is incomplete, stale, contradictory, version-skewed, unverified, or inconsistent with product behavior and release evidence."
documentation_clean_replacement_rule: "Remove superseded guidance after its replacement and all consuming references are verified. Preserve immutable release history and failure evidence separately; obsolete instructions receive no legacy-support authority."
memory_endpoints_policy_id: memory-endpoints-two-lane-ecosystem-v1
memory_endpoints_agent_coordination_use: "Agents working on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination."
memory_endpoints_tinyrustlm_connect_use: "Separately, the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lets a user sign in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly use it as the long-term-memory provider for TinyRustLM.com Connect."
memory_endpoints_lane_boundary: "Keep direct agent coordination and the user plugin separately identified, scoped, consented, authenticated, and evidenced; neither lane silently grants authority to the other, and configured or reachable state is not live-operation proof."
memory_redundancy_rule: "During prelaunch, important memory may also be retained in current .uai, wiki, source-controlled public-safe notes, or other approved stores for resilience. Every maintained copy must stay current, provenance-labeled, secret-safe, and noncontradictory."
